# Read by BOTH kinds of deployment, which is easy to get wrong:
#   - Vercel CLI uploads (`vercel deploy`, Path B in docs/runbooks/deploy.md) filter the working
#     tree through this file plus the CLI's own built-in list, and never through .gitignore.
#   - Git-triggered deployments clone the repository and then apply this file too. The build log for
#     6e0a87a reports "Found .vercelignore (repository root)" and "Removed 2 ignored files defined
#     in .vercelignore /.vscode/extensions.json /.vscode/settings.json".
# The CLI's built-in list covers node_modules, .next, .git, .env.local, .env.*.local, .DS_Store,
# npm-debug.log and a few more, so everything else that the root .gitignore and the two
# apps/*/.gitignore files exclude is repeated below. .turbo matters most: its cache tarballs exceed
# Vercel's 100 MB per-file upload limit, and the first Path B attempt failed on 1.9 GB of it.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore's, so a leading slash anchors a pattern to the repository root. Every
# directory pattern here is anchored to where that directory is actually produced: an unanchored
# `build`, `dist` or `out` would also strip a tracked source directory of that name at any depth.
# Add a line when an app is added; nothing checks this file against the .gitignore files it mirrors.

# Turborepo caches: one at the root, one per app.
/.turbo
/apps/web/.turbo
/apps/playground/.turbo
/.pnpm-store

# Build output. .next is on the CLI's built-in list; .next-e2e is the local e2e dist dir (ADR 0014).
/apps/web/.next-e2e
/apps/web/out
/apps/web/build
/apps/playground/dist
/build
/out
/dist

# Test output.
/apps/web/coverage
/apps/web/test-results
/apps/web/playwright-report
/.playwright-mcp

# Environment files. apps/web/.gitignore ignores `.env*`; the CLI's built-in list covers only
# .env.local and .env.*.local, so `apps/web/.env.production` would otherwise be uploaded. The
# tracked .env.example is kept, which is why this is not a bare `.env*`.
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem

# Generated type and build metadata.
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Editor, OS and agent state. .remember holds session logs (~1.4 MB) and is hidden from git only by
# its own untracked .gitignore, so a root `vercel deploy` would upload it.
/.idea
/.vscode
/.vercel
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.worktrees
/.claude/worktrees
.remember
*.swp
*.swo
Thumbs.db
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
